<div class="help-prose">
    <div class="help-callout"><strong>In an emergency, contact emergency services directly.</strong><p>Do not wait for a support reply, an app notification, or a map update when someone is in danger.</p></div>
    <section><h4>1. What PyroSense provides</h4><p>PyroSense supports fire incident reporting, station coordination, prevention planning, and public safety information. Available features depend on your account role and the participating station. Submitting a report is not a guarantee that a crew has been dispatched or that assistance will arrive within a particular time.</p></section>
    <section><h4>2. Report what you actually know</h4><p>Give the clearest location, nearby landmark, and incident details you can safely provide. Distinguish what you observed from what someone told you. Do not submit deliberately false reports, impersonate responders, upload unrelated material, or interfere with dispatch operations. Do not approach a hazard to obtain a photo.</p></section>
    <section><h4>3. Protect your account</h4><p>Use accurate account details and keep passwords and verification codes private. Do not share staff accounts or attempt to access another person's records. If you suspect unauthorized access, change your password when possible and contact your station administrator.</p></section>
    <section><h4>4. Location, connectivity, and status updates</h4><p>GPS positions, map routes, and travel estimates can be inaccurate. Check the map pin and provide landmarks when the signal is weak. A saved offline report is not the same as a successfully submitted report. Connection loss, maintenance, or stale data can delay updates; a truck marker alone does not confirm a responder's physical arrival.</p></section>
    <section><h4>5. Forecasts support human decisions</h4><p>Risk forecasts and AI-generated recommendations are estimates based on available information, not a guarantee that a fire will or will not occur. Authorized personnel must review recommendations before using them for operational decisions. Follow official instructions at the scene.</p></section>
    <section><h4>6. Respect other people's information</h4><p>Only upload information relevant to the incident and that you are permitted to share. Avoid unnecessary faces, identification documents, medical details, or private addresses unrelated to the report. Do not copy or publicly share restricted incident, personnel, or account records.</p></section>
    <section><h4>7. Access and service concerns</h4><p>Misuse may be referred to an authorized administrator for review and access restrictions. If you believe a restriction or record is incorrect, ask your administrator to review it. Availability and features may change; these terms do not remove rights or protections provided by applicable Philippine law.</p></section>
    <section><h4>8. Questions about these terms</h4><p>Use the support contact shown in PyroSense, or ask the station administering your account to identify the project operator. Support inquiries are separate from emergency reports.</p></section>
</div>
